From 7cdcd5f4ae1c08f6c098def712f3039023d3eaad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwan-uschka <iwan@creativytool.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:42:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Generate NOTICE.md's third-party manifest from
 bundle-ghostscript.sh's actual Homebrew closure

Issue #7: the hand-maintained manifest could silently drift from what a
release actually bundles as dependency versions change. bundle-ghostscript.sh
now attributes every bundled library back to its Homebrew formula, harvests
each project's own license file into licenses/<project>/ in the output tree,
and regenerates NOTICE.md's generated block from that data (version, SPDX
license, homepage, bundled files, license files) instead of relying on prose.
---
 NOTICE.md                              |  22 ++-
 README.md                              |  23 ++-
 scripts/bundle-ghostscript.sh          | 105 ++++++++++-
 scripts/lib/ghostscript-thirdparty.sh  | 135 ++++++++++++++
 scripts/make_test.sh                   |   4 +
 scripts/test-ghostscript-thirdparty.sh | 240 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 516 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 scripts/lib/ghostscript-thirdparty.sh
 create mode 100755 scripts/test-ghostscript-thirdparty.sh

